{
  "name": "ResponseGrid (sequential)",
  "description": "Sequential emergency incident command: 5 specialists, each with its own Hotdata database, merged by an incident commander.",
  "version": 1,
  "source": "incident_feed",
  "components": [
    {
      "id": "incident_feed",
      "provider": "webhook",
      "name": "Incident feed",
      "config": {
        "type": "webhook",
        "mode": "Source",
        "hideForm": true,
        "parameters": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hazard",
      "provider": "agent_rocketride",
      "name": "FIRE / HAZARD",
      "config": {
        "agent_description": "FIRE / HAZARD specialist for hazard intelligence",
        "instructions": [
          "You are one specialist inside an emergency incident-command system. Your data lives in your OWN database; query it with SQL before answering. Tables are addressed as default.main.<table>. The SQL surface is READ-ONLY. All data is SIMULATED for an exercise. Answer with ONE JSON object and nothing else: no prose, no code fences. Be terse: short strings, no restating the question, at most 5 items per list. Cite the row ids you relied on.",
          "Own active hazard zones, fire spread and direction, wind and weather, threatened areas, and immediate hazard priorities.",
          "Query hazards for spread_rate_mph/bearing_deg/containment, weather for wind, and zones for who is threatened. Rank by structures_at_risk and spread rate.",
          "Return exactly this JSON shape: {\"active_zones\":[{\"hazard_id\":\"\",\"name\":\"\",\"severity\":\"extreme|high|moderate|low\",\"spread\":\"\",\"threatens\":\"\"}],\"wind\":{\"from_deg\":0,\"gust_mph\":0,\"effect\":\"\"},\"priority_actions\":[{\"action\":\"\",\"why\":\"\",\"hazard_id\":\"\"}],\"zones_to_evacuate_first\":[\"\"],\"cited_ids\":[\"\"],\"confidence\":\"high|medium|low\"}"
        ],
        "max_waves": 3,
        "agent_rocketride": {
          "profile": "default"
        },
        "parameters": {}
      },
      "input": [
        {
          "lane": "questions",
          "from": "incident_feed"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "llm_hazard",
      "provider": "llm_anthropic",
      "name": "Claude (claude-haiku-4-5)",
      "config": {
        "profile": "claude-haiku-4-5",
        "claude-haiku-4-5": {
          "apikey": "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY}"
        },
        "apikey": "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY}",
        "parameters": {}
      },
      "control": [
        {
          "classType": "llm",
          "from": "hazard"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "mem_hazard",
      "provider": "memory_internal",
      "config": {
        "type": "memory_internal",
        "parameters": {}
      },
      "control": [
        {
          "classType": "memory",
          "from": "hazard"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "hd_hazard",
      "provider": "db_hotdata",
      "name": "Hotdata hazard",
      "config": {
        "profile": "default",
        "hotdata": {
          "apikey": "${HOTDATA_API_KEY}",
          "workspace_id": "${HOTDATA_WORKSPACE_ID}",
          "database_id": "${HOTDATA_DB_HAZARD}",
          "allow_execute": true,
          "allow_destructive_load": false,
          "db_description": "Tables in default.main: hazards, weather, zones. All rows are simulated exercise data. Domain: hazard intelligence.",
          "max_execute_rows": 2000,
          "job_timeout_secs": 60,
          "max_attempts": 2
        },
        "hotdata.apikey": "${HOTDATA_API_KEY}",
        "hotdata.workspace_id": "${HOTDATA_WORKSPACE_ID}",
        "hotdata.database_id": "${HOTDATA_DB_HAZARD}",
        "hotdata.allow_execute": true,
        "hotdata.allow_destructive_load": false,
        "hotdata.db_description": "Tables in default.main: hazards, weather, zones. All rows are simulated exercise data. Domain: hazard intelligence.",
        "hotdata.max_execute_rows": 2000,
        "hotdata.job_timeout_secs": 60,
        "hotdata.max_attempts": 2,
        "parameters": {}
      },
      "control": [
        {
          "classType": "tool",
          "from": "hazard"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "evacuation",
      "provider": "agent_rocketride",
      "name": "EVACUATION + TRAFFIC",
      "config": {
        "agent_description": "EVACUATION + TRAFFIC specialist for evacuation and traffic",
        "instructions": [
          "You are one specialist inside an emergency incident-command system. Your data lives in your OWN database; query it with SQL before answering. Tables are addressed as default.main.<table>. The SQL surface is READ-ONLY. All data is SIMULATED for an exercise. Answer with ONE JSON object and nothing else: no prose, no code fences. Be terse: short strings, no restating the question, at most 5 items per list. Cite the row ids you relied on.",
          "Own evacuation zones, road status, closures, congestion, routing, bottlenecks and alternate corridors.",
          "Compare current_flow_vph against capacity_vph to find bottlenecks. Note any route that is the ONLY egress for a zone, and which shelters routes can reach.",
          "Return exactly this JSON shape: {\"bottlenecks\":[{\"route_id\":\"\",\"utilization_pct\":0,\"issue\":\"\"}],\"recommended_routes\":[{\"zone_id\":\"\",\"route_id\":\"\",\"to_facility\":\"\",\"note\":\"\"}],\"closures\":[{\"route_id\":\"\",\"reason\":\"\"}],\"single_points_of_failure\":[{\"route_id\":\"\",\"zone_id\":\"\",\"risk\":\"\"}],\"priority_actions\":[{\"action\":\"\",\"why\":\"\"}],\"cited_ids\":[\"\"],\"confidence\":\"high|medium|low\"}"
        ],
        "max_waves": 3,
        "agent_rocketride": {
          "profile": "default"
        },
        "parameters": {}
      },
      "input": [
        {
          "lane": "answers",
          "from": "hazard"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "llm_evacuation",
      "provider": "llm_anthropic",
      "name": "Claude (claude-haiku-4-5)",
      "config": {
        "profile": "claude-haiku-4-5",
        "claude-haiku-4-5": {
          "apikey": "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY}"
        },
        "apikey": "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY}",
        "parameters": {}
      },
      "control": [
        {
          "classType": "llm",
          "from": "evacuation"
        }
      ]
    },
