      "id": "mem_evacuation",
      "provider": "memory_internal",
      "config": {
        "type": "memory_internal",
        "parameters": {}
      },
      "control": [
        {
          "classType": "memory",
          "from": "evacuation"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "hd_evacuation",
      "provider": "db_hotdata",
      "name": "Hotdata evacuation",
      "config": {
        "profile": "default",
        "hotdata": {
          "apikey": "${HOTDATA_API_KEY}",
          "workspace_id": "${HOTDATA_WORKSPACE_ID}",
          "database_id": "${HOTDATA_DB_EVACUATION}",
          "allow_execute": true,
          "allow_destructive_load": false,
          "db_description": "Tables in default.main: routes, zones, weather, facilities. All rows are simulated exercise data. Domain: evacuation and traffic.",
          "max_execute_rows": 2000,
          "job_timeout_secs": 60,
          "max_attempts": 2
        },
        "hotdata.apikey": "${HOTDATA_API_KEY}",
        "hotdata.workspace_id": "${HOTDATA_WORKSPACE_ID}",
        "hotdata.database_id": "${HOTDATA_DB_EVACUATION}",
        "hotdata.allow_execute": true,
        "hotdata.allow_destructive_load": false,
        "hotdata.db_description": "Tables in default.main: routes, zones, weather, facilities. All rows are simulated exercise data. Domain: evacuation and traffic.",
        "hotdata.max_execute_rows": 2000,
        "hotdata.job_timeout_secs": 60,
        "hotdata.max_attempts": 2,
        "parameters": {}
      },
      "control": [
        {
          "classType": "tool",
          "from": "evacuation"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "medical",
      "provider": "agent_rocketride",
      "name": "MEDICAL + SHELTER",
      "config": {
        "agent_description": "MEDICAL + SHELTER specialist for medical and sheltering",
        "instructions": [
          "You are one specialist inside an emergency incident-command system. Your data lives in your OWN database; query it with SQL before answering. Tables are addressed as default.main.<table>. The SQL surface is READ-ONLY. All data is SIMULATED for an exercise. Answer with ONE JSON object and nothing else: no prose, no code fences. Be terse: short strings, no restating the question, at most 5 items per list. Cite the row ids you relied on.",
          "Own hospitals, emergency capacity, ambulances, shelters and shelter capacity, vulnerable populations, and evacuation destination constraints.",
          "Sum available beds and shelter headroom against zones.vulnerable_residents. Flag any facility above 85% occupancy and any care facility needing transport.",
          "Return exactly this JSON shape: {\"hospital_status\":[{\"facility_id\":\"\",\"available\":0,\"concern\":\"\"}],\"shelter_plan\":[{\"facility_id\":\"\",\"available\":0,\"assign_zones\":\"\",\"note\":\"\"}],\"vulnerable_population\":[{\"zone_id\":\"\",\"count\":0,\"need\":\"\"}],\"transport_needs\":[{\"facility_id\":\"\",\"units_needed\":0,\"kind\":\"\"}],\"priority_actions\":[{\"action\":\"\",\"why\":\"\"}],\"cited_ids\":[\"\"],\"confidence\":\"high|medium|low\"}"
        ],
        "max_waves": 3,
        "agent_rocketride": {
          "profile": "default"
        },
        "parameters": {}
      },
      "input": [
        {
          "lane": "answers",
          "from": "evacuation"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "llm_medical",
      "provider": "llm_anthropic",
      "name": "Claude (claude-haiku-4-5)",
      "config": {
        "profile": "claude-haiku-4-5",
        "claude-haiku-4-5": {
